From cf270f4ac5e7a473a8a15afb31a2cc497549f2b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:17:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: name the .aon sources by their extension
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the .aon rename: spec/*.aontu became spec/*.aon, but this
workflow still calls them .aontu in two comments, the spec-freshness job's
display name, and the message printed when the artifact is stale.

Cosmetic only. No CI logic keys off the extension — the job runs `make spec`
and diffs `git status --porcelain -- spec/` — so it has been passing on the
renamed sources throughout; it just reports them under the old name.

Carried as a patch because pushing .github/workflows/ needs a `workflow`
scoped token, which the session that did the rename did not have.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 9f97e0a..799176d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -60,11 +60,11 @@ jobs:
       # A guard that has never failed is not a guard.
       - name: The guard must catch what it claims to
         run: python3 tools/omni_isolation_selftest.py
-  # spec/sekreto.json is generated from spec/*.aontu and committed so that
+  # spec/sekreto.json is generated from spec/*.aon and committed so that
   # no port needs a Node toolchain. Recompile it here and fail if the
   # committed copy differs — a spec edit cannot land with a stale artifact.
   spec-freshness:
-    name: spec regenerates from *.aontu
+    name: spec regenerates from *.aon
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7
@@ -73,14 +73,14 @@ jobs:
           node-version: '24'
       - run: make spec
       # Not `git diff --exit-code`: that ignores untracked files, so a commit
-      # adding a new spec/*.aontu without its generated JSON would pass while
+      # adding a new spec/*.aon without its generated JSON would pass while
       # the artifact the ports read was never committed at all.
       - name: Fail if a committed spec JSON is stale or missing
         run: |
           if [ -n "$(git status --porcelain -- spec/)" ]; then
             git status --porcelain -- spec/
             echo
-            echo "spec/ is out of sync with its .aontu sources."
+            echo "spec/ is out of sync with its .aon sources."
             echo "Run 'make spec' and commit the result."
             exit 1
           fi
-- 
